Entries for the Illinois QSO Party used by in-state (Illinois) stations
The 102 Illinois counties (each its own multiplier), the US states with DC counted as Maryland, and the 13 Canadian provinces and territories.
DXCC countries other than the USA, Canada, Hawaii and Alaska are the class's DX multiplier (at most 5 in the score), not entries here.
The county file comes FIRST, so a county code wins over any state or province alias spelled the same.
DC is mapped to Md before S50.DOM: the rules count US states, and NY4I ruled DC counts as Maryland (issue 119).
IL itself stays on the state list: an Illinois county QSO also earns it (the class, issue 317), and so does a station logged as IL (NY4I, issue 119).
Every key here longer than two letters is a county: the class's county-earns-IL rule relies on it.
NF and LB are read as NL (the last line).
No line of this header may hold an equals sign: the reader takes any such line as an entry.

INCLUDE FILE illinois_cty.dom
Dc > Md = DC
INCLUDE FILE s50.dom
INCLUDE FILE p13.dom
Nl = NF,LB
